  "security_implications": "sw_binding_unlock_o is a critical security gate that releases key material binding only on a successful advance with no errors. If op_err or op_fault_err are masked, or if op_ack/error timing glitches occur, binding could be unlocked prematurely, exposing secret keys. The dis_op decoding treats any undefined op_i as a disable, which could be exploited by an attacker to force a disable/wipe transition. invalid_kmac_out checks data integrity of KMAC output; a bypass or glitch in this check could allow corrupted key material to propagate into key state. The update_sel priority mux ensures wipe/random take precedence, but a priority error or race could cause incorrect key updates. The sparse FSM encoding relies on state_q staying within defined encodings; a single-bit flip could produce an invalid state, potentially enabling unauthorized operations.",
  "evidence_refs": [
    "keymgr_ctrl.sv:109-245"
  ],
